"A309563 - OEIS (https://oeis.org/A309563)\nciteturn4search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7.3 years ago; Crawled: last month; Miklos Bona and Michael Cory, Cyclic Permutations Avoiding Pairs of Patterns of Length Three, arXiv:1805.05196 [math.CO], 2018-2019. ... a(4) = 1, since the only cyclic permutation of length 4 avoiding both 123 and 231 is (4231) = 4312.\n\n(Greetings from The On-Line Encyclopedia of Integer Sequences!)\n\nA309563\n\nNumber of cyclic permutations of length n that avoid the patterns 123 and 231.\n\n1\n\n1, 1, 1, 1, 2, 3, 2, 2, 4, 6, 2, 2, 6, 8, 4, 4, 6, 10, 4, 4, 10, 12, 4, 4, 12, 18, 6, 6, 8, 12, 8, 8, 16, 22, 6, 6, 18, 22, 8, 8, 12, 22, 10, 10, 22, 26, 8, 8, 20, 32, 12, 12, 18, 24, 12, 12, 28, 36, 8, 8, 30, 38, 16, 16, 20, 36, 16, 16, 24, 30, 12, 12, 36, 54\n\nOFFSET\n\n1,5\n\nLINKS\n\nPaolo Xausa, Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000\n\nMiklos Bona and Michael Cory, Cyclic Permutations Avoiding Pairs of Patterns of Length Three, arXiv:1805.05196 [math.CO], 2018-2019.\n\nFORMULA\n\na(2) = 1; a(n) = phi(n/2) if n = 4k, a(n) = phi((n+2)/4) + phi(n/2) if n = 4k+2 > 2, and a(n) = phi((n+1)/2) if n is odd, where phi is the Euler totient function.\n\nSum_{k=1..n} a(k) ~ (27/(16*Pi^2)) * n^2. - Amiram Eldar, Sep 08 2026\n\nEXAMPLE\n\na(4) = 1, since the only cyclic permutation of length 4 avoiding both 123 and 231 is (4231) = 4312.\n\nMATHEMATICA\n\nA309563[n_] := Which[n < 5, 1, OddQ[n], EulerPhi[(n+1)/2], True, EulerPhi[n/2] + If[Divisible[n, 4], 0, EulerPhi[(n+2)/4]]];\n\nArray[A309563, 100] (* Paolo Xausa, Oct 17 2025 *)\n\nPROG\n\n(PARI) a(n) = if (n%2, eulerphi((n+1)/2), if (n==2, 1, if (n%4, eulerphi((n+2)/4) + eulerphi(n/2), eulerphi(n/2)))); \\\\ Michel Marcus, Oct 16 2025\n\nCROSSREFS\n\nCf. A000010.\n\nSequence in context: A372053 A053269 A163873 * A292588 A335965 A225176\n\nAdjacent sequences: A309560 A309561 A309562 * A309564 A309565 A309566\n\nKEYWORD\n\nnonn,easy\n\nAUTHOR\n\nMiklos Bona, Aug 07 2019\n\nSTATUS\n\napproved----------------