\\right|\\ge 1. Therefore, u has a large second neighborhood in D, which is a contradiction. This proves that {D}^{\\prime } contains at least two vertices with large second neighborhoods. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA309506 - OEIS (https://oeis.org/A309506)\nciteturn4search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7.3 years ago; Crawled: last year; Miklos Bona and Michael Cory, Cyclic Permutations Avoiding Pairs of Patterns of Length Three, arXiv:1805.05196 [math.CO], 2018.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nau:Cory_M in:math - SciRate Search (https://scirate.com/search?q=au%3ACory_M+in%3Amath)\nciteturn4search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; We find a closed expression for the number of permutation graphs dominated by a set with two elements, and we find a closed expression for the number of permutation graphs efficiently dominated by any set of vertices. ... @misc{1805.05196, author = {Miklos Bona and Michael Cory}, title = {{C}yclic permutations avoiding pairs of patterns of length three}, year = {2018}, eprint = {1805.05196}, note = {arXiv:1805.05196v5} }[Button: Copy Citation] ... We also prove a lower bound for the growth rate of the number of cyclic permutations that avoid a single pattern $q$, where $q$ is an element of a certain infinite family of patterns.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA309505 - OEIS (https://oeis.org/A309505)\nciteturn4search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7.3 years ago; Crawled: last year; Number of cyclic permutations of length n that avoid the pattern 132 (equivalently, 213). ... Miklos Bona and Michael Cory, Cyclic Permutations Avoiding Pairs of Patterns of Length Three, arXiv:1805.05196 [math.CO], 2018.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA309508 - OEIS (https://oeis.org/A309508)\nciteturn4search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last year; T